      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the shirtless_man as the person engaging in absurd behaviors",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the shirtless_man, who is visually depicted as the subject of the meme's commentary. The user identifies with or imagines themselves as the man performing the actions described in the text overlays ('puts sock on doorknob', 'sleeps with a blow-up doll'), thereby projecting their own identity or behavior onto this visual representation. This projection is implicit, as there are no explicit deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you', but the meme's structure invites the viewer to see themselves as the subject of the humor or judgment.",
